    "note": "17-character Model Option Table string beginning with the fixed prefix 0300G. Calibrated entirely against the ordering-information Model Option Table (WI-0642, conventional terminal blocks) and cross-checked against WI-1744 (connectorized variant, same column layout); the device has no drawing layers (model_to_layers.has_layers=false) and no genuine part number was found in the RDB uploads or instruction manual, so no positions could be anchored to a real string. Two digits are always fixed: position 10 (Secondary Input Voltage = 2) and position 17 (trailing X). Firmware feature set (position 6) corresponds to the -0/-1/-2/-3 model suffix. The I/O board digit (position 7) and the high-interrupting-current indicator (position 12) are separate columns: 0/1 = conventional terminal blocks, W/Y = connectorized plug-in connectors. NOTE: the model_to_drawings block in this metadata references the high-I/C 2/6 digit as position_15, but both WI-0642 and WI-1744 place it at MOT column 12 (positions 15/16 are Communications Protocol / Conformal Coat); model_to_drawings position_15 appears to be an index mistake.",
